   "note": "Designed a translationally invariant ansatz block to respect the permutation symmetry of the graph connectivity problem. The block consists of single-qubit rotations (RY then RX) followed by a ring of CNOTs, repeated twice. By tying parameters (p_i) to qubit i, the block commutes with the cyclic permutation of qubits (generator [1,2,3,4,5,0]). This reduces the effective parameter space and guides the model to learn features dependent on the graph structure (e.g., connectivity patterns) rather than specific node indices, which is crucial for generalizing the 'fully connected' property. The ring topology of CNOTs ensures information flows across all nodes, facilitating the detection of global connectivity properties.",
